Next I’m adding a cheap diagonal moment-propagation estimate and blending a small amount into the Monte Carlo final layer. It is biased because it drops cross-neuron covariance, but it has no sampling noise, so a small blend can improve MSE if the bias is not too aligned with the MC error.
